<title>FRANCE: CDR sold Fonciere Euris stake to Euris.</title>
<headline>CDR sold Fonciere Euris stake to Euris.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Consortium de Realisation (CDR) said in a statement it had sold its 21.4 percent stake in Fonciere Euris and a 6.5 percent stake in Euris to unlisted parent Euris.</p>
<p>CDR is the state holding group selling assets formerly held by bank Credit Lyonnais.  </p>
<p>Fonciere Euris holds 59.40 percent of retailer Rallye, whose subsidiaries include Casino, Go Sport and Athlete's Foot.</p>
<p>Market sources had earlier speculated about the CDR sale, noting two block trade s for 1.22 million and 492,000 Fonciere Euris shares were exchanged on Monday.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
